wifi: mt76: mt7996: fix chain config for 2x2/3x3/3x3 (233) FEM variant

Factory-programmed efuse on some mixed-FEM designs reports the
antenna configuration as 4x4:4SS instead of the board's actual
2x2/3x3/3x3 layout, which mt7996_mcu_set_eeprom() then propagates
into the live EEPROM buffer sent to firmware. Override the 8 bytes
at EEPROM offset 0x190 with the correct TYPE_233 values when this
mismatch is detected, so firmware initializes chains/streams to
match the real hardware rather than the misreported efuse value.

Gated to the specific board (ASUS ZenWiFi BT8 / RT-BE14000) via DT
compatible string: we have only confirmed the factory-wrong efuse
signature on this exact unit, and have not been able to verify the
precise "before" byte pattern to key off of instead. Until that is
confirmed on other hardware, this must not run unconditionally on
every mt7996 device using this driver.

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c	2026-08-21 14:28:12.559043584 +0300
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c	2026-08-23 19:18:33.315332668 +0300
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
 #include <linux/fs.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include "mt7996.h"
 #include "mcu.h"
 #include "mac.h"
@@ -4550,6 +4551,18 @@
 			     FIELD_PREP(PAGE_IDX_MASK, i) | EE_FORMAT_WHOLE;
 		req.buf_len = cpu_to_le16(eep_len);
 
+		if (i == 0 && of_machine_is_compatible("asus,zenwifi-bt8-ubootmod")) {
+			/* ASUS ZenWiFi BT8 (BE14000): board is 2x2/3x3/3x3 (233),
+			 * but factory efuse MT_EE_WIFI_CONF claims 4x4:4SS (444).
+			 * Override with official mt7996_eeprom_233.bin reference
+			 * values (path/stream/FEM) from mtk-openwrt-feeds.
+			 * Gated to this specific board via DT compatible string --
+			 * we have not confirmed the exact factory-wrong efuse
+			 * signature on other hardware, so this must not run
+			 * unconditionally on other mt7996 devices. */
+			memcpy(eep + 0x190, "\x11\x13\x1b\x1a\x13\x1b\x08\x08", 8);
+		}
+
 		skb_put_data(skb, &req, sizeof(req));
 		skb_put_data(skb, eep, eep_len);
 
